1. **Motivation-experiment gap**: Paper claims full calibration is "intractable in high dimensions (d > 1)" yet all experiments use d=1 regression. The self-orthogonality result for d > 1 is never empirically tested.
2. **Linearity assumption**: Requires utility linear in outcomes, excluding risk-averse decision makers in the "high-stakes" domains (healthcare, finance) highlighted in the introduction.
