### QC-MAPPO Paper Overview

The paper proposes a hybrid quantum-classical MARL algorithm (QC-MAPPO) that uses quantum variational circuits to model inter-agent correlations. It provides a theoretical framework based on Total Correlation and demonstrates empirical gains on SMAC benchmarks, while transparently reporting the 25× computational overhead.

### Comparison on Key Dimensions

**Novelty:**

The QC-MAPPO paper has **moderate novelty** - the TC-grounded theoretical framework is genuine, but the algorithmic contribution (inserting a variational circuit into MAPPO) is incremental. The claimed "disentangling quantum effects" contribution was never delivered.

