## Comparative Analysis

### Paper Overview
This paper conducts an ablation study of Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO), finding that (1) negative feedback via advantage estimation is essential while (2) PPO-style clipping is unnecessary. The authors propose RGRA (REINFORCE with Group Relative Advantage), which removes clipping but retains group-relative advantages and KL regularization. Experiments on mathematical benchmarks show RGRA outperforming GRPO on 17 of 27 comparisons across small models (0.5B-1.5B).

### Comparison with Calibration Examples

