The paper addresses an important and under-explored problem with thoughtful expert annotation, but the VADER-based selection creates a fundamental confound that partially invalidates the central empirical claim about text vs. visual modality. Combined with very low inter-annotator agreement on several emotion categories (making those benchmark targets unreliable) and missing quantitative evaluation for the grounding task, this places the paper in the 3.0-4.0 range of the calibration set—above papers with fundamental architectural or methodological flaws (1.3), comparable to benchmarks with significant confounds (VocSim at 3.0), but below papers with more comprehensive evaluation or better-controlled methodology (4.5+).
