The sign inconsistency is more severe than CoRA's nomenclature issue and comparable to PBRR's theory-practice gap. The missing placement ablation prevents validation of the core architectural claim. Combined with overclaimed results and missing statistical rigor, this places LoRA-Mixer in the **4.5-5.0 range**.

Given the fundamental nature of the sign error (which invalidates the stated mechanism for specialization) and the missing critical ablation, I score this paper **4.5**, between CoRA (similar issues, 4.5) and PBRR (stronger empirical work despite theory gap, 5.0).

