The paper proposes CCAT (Classifier-Constrained Alternating Training) to address modality imbalance in multimodal learning. It identifies that alternating training methods fail to prevent classifier bias toward faster-converging modalities, and proposes a two-stage framework: (1) pretrain an unbiased classifier with cross-attention and modality-contribution regularization, then (2) freeze this classifier during alternating encoder training with LoRA modules and secondary updates for severely imbalanced samples.

