**Against 7.0+ papers** (worldinworld 7.0, hubble 7.5, pi3/textto3d/quantum 8.0):
These papers had strong novelty/paradigm shifts and cleaner core contributions despite methodological issues. worldinworld (7.0) had no statistical significance testing and planning framework gaps, but introduced a paradigm shift in world model evaluation. VT-WM's contribution is more incremental (adding tactile to vision-only models) and the missing tactile prediction evaluation undermines the core claim more severely than worldinworld's missing error bars.

